description:
Design a control unit for a simple processor architecture that decodes a 32-bit instruction input. This module determines the control signals for register write enable (RegWr), register destination (RegDst), immediate extension operation (ExtOp), ALU source selection (ALUSrc), ALU operation codes (ALUOp), branch control (Branch), memory write enable (MemWr), and memory-to-register selection (MemToReg). The output signals are predominantly constant or derived from the instruction bits, specifically setting RegDst based on specific instruction field bits and grounding other control lines, indicating a minimalistic instruction set management without enabling memory operations or branching.
module top_module(instr, RegWr, RegDst, ExtOp, ALUSrc, ALUOp, Branch,
     MemWr, MemToReg);

